<!-- BEGIN: Project Knowledge Protocol (managed by the llm-wiki skill) -->

This repository keeps a verified knowledge map under `wiki/`. Before making a non-trivial change:

1. Read `wiki/index.md` (not the whole wiki — just the index, then the relevant pages it points to).
2. Verify any claim you rely on against the actual code — the wiki is a navigation aid, source code is the authority when they disagree.
3. Check `wiki/decisions/` for relevant recorded decisions.

After a change that affects behavior, architecture, an API, the data model, configuration, or security, update the relevant `wiki/**` pages to match (cite evidence — file paths, symbols, tests — don't invent content). Skip this for purely cosmetic or formatting changes.

See `AGENTS.md` at the repo root for the full version of this instruction, and `wiki/README.md` for conventions (frontmatter schema, `[!INFERENCE]` / `[!NEEDS-VERIFICATION]` / `[!CONTRADICTION]` callouts).

<!-- END: Project Knowledge Protocol (managed by the llm-wiki skill) -->
